{
  "raw": {
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205668": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Manufacturing",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor - Manufacturing SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor - Manufacturing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor - Manufacturing Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: SUNY EOC Locations: Syracuse, NY Posted: Oct 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Position ID: 205668 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Adjunct Instructor - Manufacturing Budget Title: Adjunct Instructor Unit: UUP Professional Rank and Salary Range: $55.00/hour | 20 hours per week Duration: Academic Year -1-year appointment *This position is located in Syracuse, NY (Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center) Brief Description of Duties: The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (SEOC) is seeking Adjunct Manufacturing Instructor to provide hands-on and classroom instruction to diverse set of adult learners preparing for careers in the manufacturing industry. The instructor will deliver practical, project-based training that develops foundational manufacturing skills, technical competencies, safety practices, and workplace readiness. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Deliver engaging, hands-on instruction in fundamental manufacturing topics based on program curriculum, including: Manufacturing processes and production fundamentals Workplace and industrial safety Precision measurement and basic manufacturing math Hand and power tools, equipment, and proper tool usage Blueprint and technical drawing interpretation Quality control and inspection fundamentals Basic mechanical and industrial systems Lean manufacturing, productivity, and continuous improvement concepts Workplace professionalism, teamwork, and communication Provide hands-on demonstrations and supervise students during manufacturing lab activities. Prepare lesson plans, demonstrations, and instructional activities aligned with the Manufacturing program curriculum and established course objectives. Reinforce proper safety procedures and ensure students follow established safety requirements when using tools, machinery, and equipment. Maintain a safe, organized, and productive classroom and lab environment. Track attendance, student progress, assessments, and grades. Collaborate with faculty and staff to support student learning, skill development, program completion, and workforce readiness. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Demonstrated hands-on experience in manufacturing, production, industrial technology, machining, or a related field. Ability to provide and supervise hands-on manufacturing instruction in classroom and lab settings. Strong knowledge of manufacturing processes, industrial safety, measurement, basic manufacturing math, tools and equipment, quality practices, and blueprint/technical drawing interpretation. Ability to safely demonstrate the operation and use of applicable manufacturing tools and equipment. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
