    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203254": {
      "title": "Adjunct Pool - Nursing Clinical Faculty",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Adjunct Pool - Nursing Clinical Faculty SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Pool - Nursing Clinical Faculty Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Pool - Nursing Clinical Faculty Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Jul 31, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Position ID: 203254 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Adjunct Nursing Faculty positions are available through the SUNY Morrisville main campus and / or Norwich campus. The SUNY Morrisville nursing department includes an ACEN accredited Associate's degree and an RN-BS nursing program. Adjunct assignments are dependent on need and may include taking students into clinical rotations in long-term care, medical-surgical, psychiatric, and / or obstetrical nursing areas.  Adjunct assignments may also include teaching theory. According to program need, various teaching modalities and hours may be necessary. This may include utilizing distance learning modalities and / or possible evening and weekend hours. Travel to off-campus sites may be required. General Responsibilities: Adjunct nursing faculty are expected to help students achieve their course appropriate student learning outcomes.  The adjunct faculty member shall be responsible for the following: teaching assigned classes/clinical groups under the guidance and supervision of the faculty of record and the nursing division director. Frequent and thorough communication between the adjunct, the clinical coordinator, and the faculty of record is required. Adjunct nursing faculty are required to maintain a thorough and up-to-date knowledge in his/her nursing practice; continue professional development; utilize evidence based practice and current technology in the performance of duties; maintain standards of professional conduct and ethics appropriate to the professional position; and fulfill other duties and responsibilities of an adjunct faculty member as outlined in the college faculty handbook Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Nursing (or hold a Bachelor's degree in Nursing and be actively pursuing a Master's degree or higher in Nursing) 2+ years clinical experience Current NYS Nursing License Current BLS CPR certification (American Heart Association) Preferred: Master's degree in Nursing Teaching experience Membership in professional organizations Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA Application Instructions: Apply online at http://www.morrisville.edu/careers.  Application materials should include cover letter, resume and three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
