    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205707": {
      "title": "Area Coordinator",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Area Coordinator SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Area Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Area Coordinator Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Residence Life Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Oct 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205707 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Area Coordinator Budget Title : Residence Hall Director Unit: Residence Life Professional Rank and Salary Range: $54,090 (SL-2) Duration: Calendar year appointment Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking an Area Coordinator to join our Residence Life team. The ideal candidate will have a passion for student learning in the co-curricular environment and appreciate the opportunities for learning that occur in a community living environment. Overseeing two residence halls, the Area Coordinator will be responsible for the overall community building direction for a first year and upper-class student hall. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Supervise two residential housing facilities Maintain presence in the halls through walk-abouts, office hours, program attendance, and interaction with residents. Maintain safety and security by reporting maintenance issues in the halls. Help students resolve roommate conflicts and facilitate room changes as needed. Learn and utilize housing software (StarRez) to manage occupancy. Hire, train, supervise, and evaluate Head Resident Assistant and Resident Assistant staff. Conduct regularly scheduled staff meetings and one-on-one meetings with H/RAs. Provide team building and skill development opportunities to student staff. Address performance issues with student staff through coaching meetings. Create positive and supportive environment to encourage student academic success and student learning. Provide appropriate campus resource referrals as needed. Address student behavioral issues through mediation and formal conduct process. Provide oversight of residential education goals for assigned buildings. Participate in rotating professional staff on-duty rotation providing 24 hour response during assigned duty shifts. Represent Residence Life on campus committees, in divisional and professional development opportunities, and recruitment events. Participate in special projects, including chairing an RA Committee focused on RA Training, RA Recruitment, Social Media, RA Recognition, etc. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution of higher education. Demonstrated peer leadership or supervision experience. Strong written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated ability to foster diverse and inclusive relationships and development of cultural sensitivity. Ability to live in a provided on-campus apartment. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, or related field. Professional or paraprofessional experience in residence life/on-campus housing OR commensurate experience in student affairs/student support. Driver's license or willingness to get one Other Skills to be Successful Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to student learning and success. Candidates that have experience working with a diverse student population that requires a high touch/support environment will receive greater consideration. We appreciate candidates who are intellectually curious and see themselves as educators outside of the classroom. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
