      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Equine Science Instructional Support Associate SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Equine Science Instructional Support Associate Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Equine Science Instructional Support Associate Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Agriculture, Business & Technology Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Oct 8, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205619 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Equine Science Instructional Support Associate Budget Title : Instructional Support Associate SL2 Unit: UUP Professional Rank and Salary Range: $54,090 Duration: 12 month Calendar Year Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a twelve-month position in the Equine Science Department assisting instructional support for various labs in breeding, stable/farm management and rehabilitation, along with day-to-day management of program horses and facility, and supervision of the students during barn duty or during summer internships.  This position works as a team member in the strategic planning process with other faculty and staff members that work in Equine Science Department. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Assist with or lead as Instructional support of various Equine Science Courses: Breeding and Rehabilitation Therapies Concentrations on Tuesday-Saturday work week. Mentoring, assisting and providing oversite of student activities Barn duty (Farm Practicum) and chores in coordination with faculty/staff. In the absence of students, ensure that the barn chores, horse management or rehabilitation therapies are completed - esp. during Weekends, School Breaks & Holidays Providing leadership to program areas, training of students and working with students throughout the year and during summer internships Ability to work with fellow equine science faculty and staff to develop and fulfill programmatic outcomes along with other programs on campus Assist with or lead in daily care and maintenance of college, rehabilitation and client horses, basic veterinary care and facilities care as necessary. Assist faculty/staff or lead laboratory courses in rehabilitation, training or handling of breeding animals Incorporate principles and practices of sound equine management as well as demonstrate self-motivation and the ability to work as a team member Assisting with clients and appropriate professionals, including but not limited to: Veterinarians, Farriers, USTA technicians, Breeding Farms, Breed Organizations and Trucking firms. Aid in development of long-term and short-term plans for the Equine Science program and develop strategies for changes and improvements in recruitment, outreach, record keeping, operations, facilities and equipment Ability to operate equipment a plus: Operate tractor, skid steer, dragging arenas, mowers, manure spreader Potential to earn a CDL or has a CDL Potential to earn a license for pesticide application on animals Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Minimum of Bachelor degree in equine science or related field, prefer Bachelor + Licensed Vet Tech Degrees, would consider Associate degree with 8 years practical experience in Breeding, Rehabilitation or Horse management. The successful candidate should have strong horse handling skills regarding safe handling of young, mature, or injured horses, be a reliable and effective communicator, and have experience in instruction on horse management or therapeutic rehabilitation modalities. An appreciation of technical education at the Associate and Bachelor of Technology degree levels. Must be able to perform moderate to heavy physical labor in occasional inclement weather conditions and be willing to work on weekends. Should also be willing to travel occasionally for recruitment events or expos. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
