    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205118": {
      "title": "Director of Human Resources",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Director of Human Resources SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Director of Human Resources Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Human Resources Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Human Resources Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $100,000.00 - $120,000.00 Position ID: 205118 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Director of Human Resources Unit: M/C Salary Range: $100,000-$120,000 commensurate with skills and years of experience. Job Description: The Director of Human Resources manages a staff that includes recruitment, benefits, and payroll. The incumbent is responsible for ensuring high quality & timely service is delivered to faculty, students and staff that meet the needs and support the college's strategic goals. The Director of Human Resource ensures the college complies with all labor agreement, SUNY rules and state & federal laws. Specific Duties & Responsibilities: Provides leadership for administration and department leaders on the development of campus-wide policies and procedures relating to employment practices as well as diversity and inclusion initiatives. Works with college administration to develop procedures to support the college's organizational strategic planning goals, including programs for ongoing professional development of faculty and staff. Works closely with department and division heads to ensure appropriate staffing for functional areas and appropriate classification and compensation within the specifications of collective bargaining agreements. Maintains supervisory responsibility for Human Resources employees. Functional areas of responsibility include: Employee relations, recruitment and retention, classification and compensation, employee benefits, payroll, performance evaluation systems, workers compensation and leave programs, reasonable accommodations under the ADA, facilitation of immigration processes for employees, and training programs and employee development. Responsibility for the administration of four separate Collective Bargaining Agreements and serving as primary contact for labor relations. Supervises the development and implementation of annual mandatory trainings. Manage faculty, staff students and college work study payroll.  Ensure compliance with applicable regulations. Provides confidential advice for faculty, staff and students. Maintains employee records and reports. Participates in SUNY HR meetings and represents Human Resources in meetings. Perform other duties and required or directed. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required, master's degree preferred. Seven or more years of experience in Human Resources or similar roles or a combination of relevant years of experience and education. Excellent & responsive communication skills and strong organizational skills required. Experience in employee relations, unionized environment preferred. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community, especially members of historically under-represented groups. AA/EEO/ADA Application Instructions: Application Deadline:  Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204998": {
      "title": "Vice President of Administration and Finance",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Vice President of Administration and Finance SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Vice President of Administration and Finance Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Vice President of Administration and Finance Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Office of the President Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Sep 18, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204998 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Vice President of Administration and Finance Budget Title : Vice President for Administration Unit: M/C 13 view our generous state benefits package here Professional Rank and Salary Range: MP1, $150,000 - $175,000 Duration: Calendar Year (this position works 12-months of the year) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville seeks a Vice President of Administration and Finance to serve both as a key member of the institution's senior leadership team and a strategic and action-oriented member of the President's Cabinet. Reporting directly to the President, the successful candidate will serve as a strategic advisor on financial, administrative, operational, and organizational matters; providing effective leadership that aids in ensuring the effective stewardship of the College's resources and the long-term fiscal and operational sustainability of the institution. The Vice President will be responsible for the College's fiscal and operational strategic priorities and day-to-day financial operations, including budgeting, financial forecasting and reporting, resource allocation, compliance, and general institutional financial planning. The Vice President will work closely with the President, Cabinet, shared governance bodies, and campus constituencies to align financial and administrative resources with the College's strategic priorities and commitment to student success. The portfolio of oversight includes the Business Office (Purchasing, Accounting & Accounts Payable), Human Resources, Facilities and Maintenance, Planning, Design and Construction, Technology Services, as well as serving as the liaison to the SUNY Research Foundation in terms of the Campus' research activities. The Vice President also works collaboratively with the Morrisville College Foundation and Morrisville Auxiliary Corporation, all while serving as a key institutional liaison with SUNY System Administration, other campuses, and external State/Local/Federal agencies and partners. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Serve as a key member of the President's Cabinet while providing strategic financial and administrative advice to the President, senior leadership team, and the campus at large. Collaborate with the President, Cabinet, faculty, staff, and other campus constituencies to develop, refine, and advance the institution's strategic goals and priorities with fiscal stability as a fundamental pillar. Direct, and participate in the development, presentation, monitoring, and adjustment of the College's operating and capital budgets, including long-term financial planning, forecasting, resource allocation, and analysis of institutional financial trends. Ensure alignment of capital budgets with strategic direction of the campus. Develop a comprehensive method to balance capital deployment with respect to front facing projects and critical maintenance related to infrastructure. Provide clear, timely, and accessible financial and operational information and analysis to the President, Cabinet, governance bodies, and other stakeholders to support informed institutional decision-making and convey the fiscal position/performance of the campus. Develop and maintain positive working relationships with a variety of stakeholders to acquire information and appropriate legal guidance, especially as it relates to funding and completing capital projects. Outside groups include SUNY System Administration; the State University Construction Fund (SUCF); Dormitory Authority of New York (DASNY); the State University Business Officers Association (SUBOA); State, Local, and / or Federal government officials; and various professional organizations. Ensure compliance with applicable SUNY System Administration, Office of the State Comptroller, State, Local, Federal, and other regulatory requirements, as well as internal controls, audit recommendations, and institutional policies. Maintain clear and consistent communication on behalf of the Business Office, ensuring that appropriate departments are made aware of campus needs, and the campus is informed about relevant activities within the division. Oversee and provide strategic leadership for Human Resources, including employee relations, recruitment and retention, compensation and classification, benefits, professional development, labor relations, personnel policies and procedures, compliance, and initiatives that support a positive, inclusive, and high-performing workplace. Provide leadership and strategic oversight for Facilities and Maintenance, Planning, Design and Construction, including capital planning, campus infrastructure, facilities operations, major projects, and the effective stewardship of College facilities and physical resources. Provide strategic oversight of capital projects, deferred maintenance, infrastructure planning, facilities operations, and related funding strategies, working closely with SUNY, SUCF, DASNY, contractors, consultants, and other partners to advance projects and ensure responsible stewardship of the College's physical assets. Provide strategic oversight of Technology Services and ensure that technology resources and investments effectively support teaching, learning, student services, administrative operations, institutional effectiveness, and long-term strategic priorities. Work collaboratively with campus leaders to assess technology needs, prioritize investments, and promote secure, sustainable, effective, and cost-conscious technology operations. Serve on the board of the Morrisville Auxiliary Corporation (MAC) as a voting member and on the Morrisville College Foundation board as a non-voting member. Oversee and participate on relevant committees including the Senate Budget Committee. Support effective relationships with the Morrisville College Foundation, Research Foundation, and other affiliated organizations and provide financial, administrative, and strategic expertise as appropriate. Identify opportunities to strengthen external partnerships, grants, auxiliary operations, fundraising, and other resources that support institutional priorities. Work collaboratively with business and industry partners, government officials, alumni, donors, community organizations, and other external stakeholders to advance the College's mission and identify opportunities for institutional and financial growth. Research, align, and implement improvements to the College's historical approach to allocating funding and personnel; work with other SUNY institutions to identify potential shared services and increased efficiencies; constantly seeking opportunities to improve efficiency and effect cost reductions. Oversee appropriate risk management, insurance, contracts, audits, internal controls, and other institutional processes designed to protect College resources and mitigate financial and operational risk. Participate in and support shared governance and collaborative decision-making. Serve on appropriate College committees, including the Senate Budget Committee and other committees as assigned. Work collaboratively with campus leadership and employee representatives to foster positive labor relations and a work environment characterized by respect, accountability, communication, professional growth, and shared commitment to student success. Maintain a visible presence on campus and participate in College events and activities, demonstrating engagement with students, faculty, staff, and the broader campus community. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the President. The Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to collaborate and support the strategic direction and decisions of the institution at the highest level, all while being able to actively engage in identifying and recommending proper allocation of the college's resources to most effectively support the achievement of identified goals, objectives and direction of the institution. Ability to understand and evaluate financial information from multiple sources that all come with various rules and regulations, codifying this understanding into sound strategic financial forecasting and recommendations to attain, and then maintain, the financial stability of the institution. Ability to understand, interpret and explain complex budget information to a wide audience, with a commitment to transparency in the sharing of information. Ability to exercise sound judgement and to include others in decision-making processes, as warranted. Experience with capital planning, prioritization of funding request for implementation that aligns with the campus master plan. Demonstrated understanding of shared governance and being able to collaboratively approach decision making with a strong focus on student centeredness. Demonstrated openness to different viewpoints and ability to communicate in a manner which demonstrates sensitivity and respect for diverse backgrounds and experiences. Demonstrate high ethical and moral standards. Demonstrated skill in developing staff, possessing flexible interpersonal styles to most effectively interact with and develop others. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in business administration, finance, accounting, public administration, higher education administration, human resources, or a related field. Progressively responsible experience in the areas of business, accounting or financial management may serve as an alternative and is highly desired. Significant progressively responsible experience (5 years+) in financial management, business administration, higher education administration, or a related field, including responsibility for budgeting, financial planning, resource allocation, and administrative operations. Demonstrated experience serving in a senior-level leadership role with responsibility for strategic planning, institutional decision-making, organizational management, and collaborative problem-solving. Demonstrated ability to lead complex organizational functions and work effectively with multiple stakeholders in a collaborative environment. Preferred Qualifications: Master of Business Administration (MBA) or comparable advanced degree. Significant leadership experience in higher education or another complex, multi-functional organization. Experience providing executive oversight for multiple administrative functions, including finance, human resources, facilities, technology, and/or operations. Experience with capital planning, facilities development, deferred maintenance, and major capital projects. Experience working within the SUNY system or another public higher education system. Experience working in a unionized environment and with collective bargaining agreements. Experience working with foundations, auxiliaries, affiliated organizations, grants, or other external funding sources. Demonstrated experience developing strategies for financial sustainability, revenue diversification, operational efficiency, and resource development. Experience leading complex organizational change and building effective partnerships across institutional and external stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204464": {
      "title": "Vice President for Inclusive Excellence/ Chief Diversity Officer",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Vice President for Inclusive Excellence/ Chief Diversity Officer SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Vice President for Inclusive Excellence/ Chief Diversity Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Vice President for Inclusive Excellence/ Chief Diversity Officer Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Office of the President Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Sep 4, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204464 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Vice President for Inclusive Excellence/ Chief Diversity Officer Budget Title : Vice President Unit: MC Professional Rank and Salary Range: $120,000 Duration: Calendar Year (12 Months) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a VP for Inclusive Excellence/ Chief Diversity Officer (CDO) to provide strategic leadership for the College's efforts to advance the State University of New York's (SUNY) Four Pillars: student success, research and scholarship, diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI), and economic development and upward mobility. This position works collaboratively across the institution to promote student and employee outcomes, strengthen an inclusive and welcoming campus climate, address achievement and opportunity gaps, and ensure that SUNY's four pillars are integrated into institutional planning, policies, practices, and decision-making. The CDO serves as a senior advisor to the President and President's Cabinet, is a member of the President's Cabinet, and serves as the College's primary liaison for SUNY initiatives and requirements that advance institutional success. The CDO also oversees compliance areas (Title VI, IX, etc.) and is responsible for ensuring that appropriate policies, training, processes, and institutional practices are in place to support compliance with applicable federal, state, and SUNY requirements. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Advise the President, Cabinet, and campus leadership on matters related to campus climate, organizational culture, belonging, and accessibility. Supervise Title IX, Title VI, Affirmative Action, and other compliance area staff. Develop, implement, assess, and continuously improve campus climate and belonging in strategic planning, institutional effectiveness, student success, and employee engagement efforts. Develop, execute and assess departmental initiatives and programs that enhance campus culture including training and professional development for faculty, staff, students, and as appropriate, external partners and community members. Coordinate campus climate assessment activities, including surveys, focus groups, listening sessions, and other methods of gathering feedback. Use climate surveys and other institutional data to identify areas of concern and recommend strategies for improvement. Serve as the College's primary point of contact for SUNY initiatives, policies, reporting requirements, and best practices related to advancing institutional success Collaborate with Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, and other campus partners to strengthen equitable practices and lead institutional efforts in recruitment, admissions, advising, student engagement, and retention. Promote a welcoming and inclusive learning and living environment in which all students feel a sense of belonging and have equitable access to educational opportunities and support services. Serve as a resource for students and campus personnel regarding concerns related to campus climate and culture. Review College policies, procedures, and practices and make recommendations or develop new policies accordingly. Lead the College's Campus Climate Committee and coordinate the development, implementation, assessment, and updating of the College's strategic plan accordingly. Collaborate with Human Resources and campus leadership to strengthen recruitment, hiring, onboarding, professional development, promotion, and retention practices. Collaborate with the Provost, Student Affairs, Human Resources, and other campus partners to integrate inclusive practices into teaching, learning, student services, and workplace environments. Maintain current knowledge of applicable laws and regulations, including Title IX, Title IV, the Clery Act, ADA, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act, and applicable nondiscrimination requirements. Develop and manage the budget and resources associated with the CDO's portfolio. Identify opportunities for external funding, partnerships, and resources that advance the College's mission-driven priorities. Develop relationships with community organizations, educational institutions, employers, government agencies, and other partners to advance the College's mission and strengthen community engagement. Supervise assigned personnel and provide leadership, direction, performance management, and professional development for direct reports. Participate in Cabinet, institutional planning, policy development, personnel discussions, and other presidential leadership activities requiring the judgment and confidentiality appropriate to a senior-level position. Perform other duties as assigned by the President. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Master's degree from an accredited institution required; doctorate preferred. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in leadership of higher education or a related educational environment, preferably within a state or community college. Demonstrated success in identifying and implementing policies and best practices as related to SUNY's four pillars (student success; research and scholarship; diversity, equity and inclusion; and economic development and upward mobility), with focused efforts on equity, inclusivity and accessibility across the entire campus population. Evidence of experience and skills in scholarly research, data analysis, assessment and knowledge/understanding relating to diversity, equity and inclusion in higher education settings. Experience with program development, strategic planning, policy development, and budget/resource management. Experience working collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, administrators, and external stakeholders. Teaching experience in higher education is preferred. Working knowledge of applicable federal and state laws, SUNY policies, and regulations related to nondiscrimination, Title IX, Title IV, Clery Act, ADA, Section 504, and related civil rights requirements. Exceptional interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. Strong strategic thinking, problem-solving, and organizational skills. Ability to manage sensitive and confidential information with discretion and sound judgment. Ability to facilitate difficult conversations and navigate complex institutional issues effectively. Proficiency with standard Microsoft Office and other technology necessary to perform the functions of the position. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204361": {
      "title": "Vice President for Student Affairs",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Vice President for Student Affairs SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Vice President for Student Affairs Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Vice President for Student Affairs Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Activities & Affairs Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Sep 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204361 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Vice President for Student Affairs Budget Title : Director Unit: M/C Professional Rank and Salary Range: $140,000 - $150,000 Duration: Calendar Year (12 Months) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a visionary leader with the experience, student affairs knowledge and interpersonal skills to be a strong advocate for students and the Division of Student Affairs. The Vice President for Student Affairs will report directly to the President and serve as a member of the President's Cabinet. They work closely with the College's staff and faculty to develop and promote a campus culture focused on student success in a safe and welcoming campus environment. The incoming Vice President for Student Affairs will be charged with leading an inclusive and participatory effort to develop a strategic vision for the Division of Student Affairs. Key priorities for the new Vice President for Student Affairs include: Advocating for students and for the Student Affairs Division. The Vice President will embrace the opportunity to champion the work of the Division. The new Vice President will pursue opportunities to set a direction for the Division that prioritizes collaborating and communicating across campus. Partnering with the Provost to enhance collaboration across divisions. A strong relationship between the Vice President for Student Affairs and the Provost is essential in promoting student success, as well as student life programs that support the academic goals of the institution. Applying strategic planning, assessment and communication skills to evaluate Divisional needs and goals. The incoming Vice President for Student Affairs is expected to provide vision in the leadership of all Student Affairs functions. A top priority will be implementing a participative process to develop a shared vision for the direction of the Division. The role will provide overall strategic direction, leadership, administration and management of the Student Affairs division, which consists of the following departments: Athletics. At SUNY Morrisville, the total college experience should be a balance of activities both in and out of the classroom. For many, sports are as much a part of college as academics. We offer the opportunity for students to get involved in a variety of intercollegiate and intramural activities. Morrisville is a member of the National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA) Division III and fields 17 intercollegiate athletic teams. Residence Life. A comfortable living environment is an important factor in the success of any college student. You'll find a range of residence halls at SUNY Morrisville, including double rooms, suites, apartments with full kitchens, single rooms and quiet-study halls. Student Activities. The Student Activities Office offers a variety of academic, cultural, recreational and social programs, events and opportunities for students to participate in at SUNY Morrisville. The student activities include more than 30 clubs, 10 organizations, intramurals, open recreation, theater, music and numerous events and services implemented throughout the Student Government Organization (SGO) and the Campus Activities Board (CAB). Events and programs offer alcohol- and drug-free alternatives for students. Student Health Services. Health Services is committed to providing confidential, high-quality, student-centered health care to SUNY Morrisville students. Student Rights and Responsibilities. The Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities is responsible for the College Judicial Affairs. The dedicated professionals within the department facilitate the student Code of Conduct so that all those on the campus community can engage in their academic program of study, gather in a safe and responsible manner, grow as individuals and live cooperatively in a civil learning environment. Title IX. Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 prohibits sex discrimination in education. These protections are not just for students; faculty and staff also are covered by the protections of Title IX. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: The successful candidate for this role will have proficiencies in multiple Student Affairs functions and an understanding of the specific areas represented in the Student Affairs portfolio, as evidenced by: A Master's degree in student affairs, student development, higher education administration or a related field. A record of effectiveness as a student affairs administrator, as evidenced by seven or more years of progressive leadership, inclusive of administrative, fiscal management and supervisory experience. Demonstrated experience supporting the retention and graduation rates of students from under-represented groups. Preferred Skills and Qualifications: Doctorate in student affairs, higher education administration or other relevant field. Evidence of success in mentoring staff and creating professional development opportunities for their advancement. Experience building relationships with and engaging the local community. Experience with crisis management, demonstrating the ability to apply sound judgment in emergency situations and to act decisively within the best interest of those involved and the College. Demonstrated commitment to and experience with nurturing DEI programs and fostering an inclusive environment. Excellent written and oral communication skills with the ability to establish and maintain a positive image for the Division and positive working relationships with internal and external constituencies. Proven organizational and leadership capabilities. Ability to work effectively with a diversity of individuals. Ability to develop a shared vision for Student Affairs that advances the strategic needs of the College and to align and organize staff and resources toward desired outcomes. Evidence of personal and professional characteristics that include integrity, creativity and flexibility. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204325": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Director of Development SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Director of Development Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Development Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Institutional Advancement Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Sep 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204325 Share About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville, a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in the center of New York State, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's 3,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state and around the world - choose from more than 50 associate and bachelor degree programs that embrace agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, including Psychology, Criminal Justice, and the liberal arts. An internship program that prepares students for success in the 21st-century workplace ranks among the top ten in the nation. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting a shrinking world with diminishing resources. The Morrisville campus is 30 miles southeast of Syracuse and 30 miles southwest of Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students associate degree options such as Criminal Justice, Computer Information Technology, and Nursing. The campus is also used by businesses, not-for-profits and community partners for training, events and videoconferencing. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the urban community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. Recognizing the importance of diversity in assuring the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment, SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. Job Description: Campus Title: Director of Development Budget Title : Staff Associate Unit: Institutional Advancement Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL4 $80,000-$90,000 Duration: Calendar Year (12 month position) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a Director of Development to oversee the planning and execution of the college's fundraising strategy.  Reporting to the Vice President for Operations, the Director will be responsible for setting and achieving goals for annual giving, leadership and major gifts, planned giving, and corporate partnerships. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Develop and implement fundraising strategies that support the mission and goals of SUNY Morrisville. Build relationships with donors, organizations and other stakeholders and increase their engagement with the college. Manage all aspects of the fundraising cycle from prospect identification to solicitation and stewardship. Provide supervision for the Senior Associate Director of Annual Giving and work collaboratively to develop and manage fundraising campaigns that align with organizational goals. Collaborate with the Foundation Board of Directors, faculty, and key staff and administrators to identify funding sources and opportunities. Develop and manage budgets for fundraising programs and initiatives. Monitor progress toward fundraising goals and provide regular reports to key stakeholders including the Board of Directors and the college community. Pursue professional development opportunities to stay current on philanthropic and nonprofit trends and best practices. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Experience in nonprofit fundraising or management with a successful track record of achieving fundraising goals. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build relationships and inspire confidence in donors and stakeholders. Excellent writing skills with the ability to write for different audiences including grant funders and prospective donors. Ability to think strategically, develop and implement plans, and manage competing priorities Passion for the mission and goals of the organization. The position will require some evening and weekend work for fundraising events and donor engagement activities. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204069": {
      "title": "Instructional Support Assistant for Automotive Technology",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Instructional Support Assistant for Automotive Technology SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Instructional Support Assistant for Automotive Technology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Instructional Support Assistant for Automotive Technology Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Agriculture, Business & Technology Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Aug 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204069 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Instructional Support Assistant for Automotive Technology Budget Title : Instructional Support Assistant Unit: UUP-08 Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL-1 / $45,000-$48,000 Duration: 10-month Academic Calendar Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking an Instructional Support Assistant (ISA) position.  This is a full time permanent position with a ten-month obligation for the Automotive Technology Programs.  The Auto Tech ISA candidate will need knowledge in A1 - A8 ASE areas with additional exposure in the service and parts advising segment of a dealership. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Primary responsibility in laboratory instruction will demand a strong dedication to hands-on, in-field instruction, and application. Additional responsibilities may include: college/university service; course and program development; program promotion; and professional development.  Additional opportunities for extra service may be available during the summer months through the offering of training and workshops.  The person filling this position will be expected to collaborate with existing faculty to utilize their expertise in developing opportunities related to automotive service/repair in mechanical and electrical systems using state-of-art technology.  The successful candidate must demonstrate teaching proficiency and possess field experience in the area of automotive service/mechanical/electrical systems.  They must also have an understanding and appreciation for technical education at the associate and baccalaureate degree levels. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: AAS Degree in Automotive Technology with 3-5 years of industry work experience required. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelors in Automotive Technology, teaching experience in a related discipline, and ASE certifications. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204068": {
      "title": "NYC Regional Admissions Recruiter",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: NYC Regional Admissions Recruiter SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: NYC Regional Admissions Recruiter Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details NYC Regional Admissions Recruiter Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Admissions Locations: New York City, NY Posted: Aug 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204068 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: NYC Regional Admissions Recruiter Budget Title : Admissions Advisor Unit: UUP Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL-3 $58,500 + Location Pay Duration: 12 months Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a dynamic and experienced Regional Admissions Recruiter - New York City to join the Admissions & Enrollment team. This full-time, remote position will serve as SUNY Morrisville's primary admissions representative throughout the New York City metropolitan area. The Regional Admissions Recruiter will play a key role in expanding SUNY Morrisville's presence in the NYC market, developing relationships with high schools, community-based organizations, counselors, prospective students and families, and generating a strong pipeline of prospective students interested in Morrisville's academic programs and career-focused educational opportunities. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Regional Recruitment & Outreach Serve as SUNY Morrisville's primary admissions representative throughout the New York City metropolitan area. Develop and implement a strategic recruitment plan for the assigned territory in collaboration with the Director of Admissions & Enrollment. Represent SUNY Morrisville at high school visits, college fairs, community-based events, college access programs, transfer events, and other recruitment activities. Establish and maintain relationships with high school counselors, administrators, community-based organizations, college access professionals, students, families, and other educational partners. Conduct individual and group admissions counseling sessions, presentations, information sessions, and virtual events. Promote SUNY Morrisville's academic programs, career-focused education, student support services, financial aid opportunities, campus experience, and pathways to employment and further education. Participate in SUNY system-wide recruitment initiatives and regional college access events. Identify opportunities to increase Morrisville's visibility and engagement within the NYC educational community. Lead Generation & Enrollment Development Develop and maintain a consistent prospective student pipeline within the assigned territory. Conduct proactive outreach to prospective students and applicants through phone, email, text messaging, virtual appointments, and other appropriate communication methods. Follow up with prospective students throughout the admissions process to encourage application completion, enrollment, and matriculation. Support yield and melt-reduction efforts by maintaining consistent communication with deposited and admitted students. Collaborate with on-campus Admissions & Enrollment staff to identify recruitment opportunities and respond to emerging enrollment trends within the territory. Identify populations, schools, organizations, and partnerships that may provide new opportunities for student recruitment. Application Review & Admissions Support Review admissions applications from students within the assigned territory in accordance with SUNY Morrisville admissions policies and procedures. Assist prospective students and families in understanding admissions requirements, application processes, deadlines, financial aid, and enrollment next steps. Maintain accurate and timely records of recruitment activities, student interactions, travel, and enrollment outcomes within the University's CRM system. Monitor territory-specific recruitment data and use that information to inform future outreach strategies. Partnership Development Develop sustainable partnerships with NYC high schools, community-based organizations, college access programs, workforce organizations, and other educational partners. Identify opportunities for articulation agreements, recruitment partnerships, group visits, and other initiatives that can strengthen Morrisville's NYC recruitment pipeline. Serve as a consistent point of contact for counselors and community partners in the assigned region. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, written and oral communication skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to travel extensively within an assigned recruitment territory and work evenings and weekends as required. Driver's License Ability to carry 40lbs Preferred Qualifications: Experience in undergraduate admissions and recruitment. Experience working with high school students, families, school counselors, community-based organizations and/or other college access partners. Experience with CRM systems and/or student information systems. Experience conducting presentations to large and small groups. Knowledge of the college admissions process and current enrollment trends. Demonstrated commitment to working with diverse student populations and fostering an inclusive environment. Additional Information: Occasional travel to SUNY Morrisville campus will be required multiple times per year for recruitment events SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
