    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203738": {
      "title": "Testing & Accessibility Services Coordinator",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Testing & Accessibility Services Coordinator SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Testing & Accessibility Services Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Testing & Accessibility Services Coordinator Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Library and Learning Resources Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Aug 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203738 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Testing & Accessibility Services Coordinator Budget Title : Instructional Support Associate Unit: UUP-08 Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL2 $53,000 per year Duration: 12 months Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a Testing & Accessibility Services Coordinator to support student success by coordinating testing services and accessibility resources. The Testing & Accessibility Services Coordinator supports the daily operations of the Testing Center and Accessibility Services. Reporting to the Director of Accessibility Services, the position coordinates, administers, and proctors accommodated and approved make-up examinations; provides operational support for the Accommodate system; supervises testing proctors and student employees; and assists faculty and students with testing and accommodation processes to ensure equitable access to educational opportunities. Primary Responsibilities: Coordinate and participate in daily Testing Center operations, including administering and proctoring accommodated and approved make-up examinations. Schedule, administer, and proctor examinations while ensuring exam security and approved accommodations.. Serve as the primary operational support person for Accommodate, assisting students and faculty with scheduling, notifications, and general system use while referring complex accommodation or compliance matters to the Director of Accessibility Services. Coordinate testing logistics with faculty, students, and campus partners to ensure secure and efficient testing operations. Recruit, train, schedule, supervise, and work alongside testing proctors and student employees to support daily Testing Center operations. Maintain testing records, documentation, and security procedures in accordance with institutional policies. Assist with Accessibility Services operations, including appointment scheduling, student communications, and general office support. Collect and maintain testing and service statistics and assist with assessment and reporting activities. Collaborate with faculty and campus partners to support testing and accessibility services. Perform other related duties as assigned in support of Accessibility Services and Libraries & Learning Resources. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in Disability Studies, Counseling, Education, Higher Education Administration, Human Services, Psychology, Social Work, or a related field. Experience: Minimum of two (2) years of professional experience in higher education, student support services, accessibility services, testing services, libraries, advising, or another student-facing environment. Skills: Ability to communicate clearly and effectively with students, faculty,  and campus partners using a variety of methods (e.g., in-person, written, and digital). Demonstrated ability to provide student-centered service in a respectful and supportive manner. Experience maintaining confidential records and handling sensitive information. Strong organizational skills with the ability to coordinate multiple priorities. Ability to learn and utilize student information and accommodation management systems. Ability to collaborate with campus partners across functional areas. Experience supervising, training, or mentoring student employees. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in accessibility services, testing centers, academic libraries, advising, or other student support environments in higher education. Experience coordinating accommodated testing or examination services. Familiarity with accessibility practices in higher education, including accommodation management systems (e.g., Accommodate) and testing management processes. Experience supporting assistive technology, testing technologies, learning technologies, or helping students access and use technology resources. Experience using student information systems and higher education technologies. SUNY Morrisville encourages applications from individuals with diverse experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. Candidates who meet most, but not all, of the qualifications are encouraged to apply. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203608": {
      "title": "HSE Program Lecturer",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: HSE Program Lecturer SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: HSE Program Lecturer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details HSE Program Lecturer Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: SUNY EOC Locations: Syracuse, NY Posted: Aug 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203608 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: HSE Program Lecturer Budget Title: Lecturer - 12 month Unit: UUP-08 Professional Rank and Salary Range: $65,000 Duration: Calendar Year (this position works year-round); 8:30am-5pm *This position is located in Syracuse, NY (Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center) Brief Description of Duties: The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (SEOC) is seeking a full-time Lecturer to provide instruction and academic support to adult learners pursuing their High School Equivalency (HSE) credential. The successful candidate will teach HSE courses, develop/update curriculum, monitor student progress, provide academic advising, and collaborate with faculty and staff to support student success. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Instruction Teach 3 High School Equivalency (HSE) courses each semester in one or more of the following subject areas: English Language Arts Mathematics Science Social Studies Develop and deliver engaging instructions that meet the needs of adult learners. Prepare lesson plans, assessments, and instructional materials. Administer and utilize academic assessments to monitor student progress. Maintain attendance, grades, and student records. Provide academic support and refer students to tutoring and other support services as needed. Student Advising Meet regularly with assigned students to monitor academic progress and support goal completion. Assist students in developing academic, career, and educational plan Connect students with available SEOC resources and student support services. Maintain accurate advising documentation. Program Support Collaborate with faculty and staff to support student success. Participate in department meetings, professional development, and program activities. Assist with student recruitment, orientation, and retention efforts. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications : Bachelor's degree in Education or a related field. (2) years of teaching experience in an educational setting. Strong classroom management, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse adult learners. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Education, Adult Education, or a related field. Experience teaching adult learners, High School Equivalency (HSE/GED), or related academic programs preferred. New York State Teaching Certification. Experience with educational assessments such as TABE or GED Ready. Bilingual or multilingual proficiency Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
