 SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Instructional Support Assistant- School of Nursing Budget Title : Instructional Support Assistant Unit: UUP-08 Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL-1 $38,500-$45,500 Duration: College year (10 month schedule) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking an Instructional Support Assistant to assist our School of Nursing Faculty, Staff, and Students. Under the direction and oversight of the Program Director of Nursing, Campus Nursing Laboratory Coordinator and SUNY Morrisville Professional Staff policies, the responsibilities of the Nursing Laboratory Staff are: Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Nursing Laboratory Support & Maintenance *Standardizes and prepares nursing lab supplies and materials (e.g., IV fluids, dressing, simulated medications) in accordance with program requirements. *Performs routine maintenance of nursing lab equipment including manikins, vital sign monitoring devices (such as blood pressure cuffs), and other equipment. *Sets up and breaks down lab stations for nursing lab teaching and practice sessions and prepares and resets equipment and environments for clinical simulations. *Assists laboratory coordinator with inventory of nursing lab supplies, consumables, and equipment; restocks labs prior to each semester. *Collaborate with the Campus Nursing Laboratory Coordinator in planning and scheduling to effectively utilize laboratory resources. *Collects and maintains statistics related to laboratory usage and communicates to the Campus Laboratory Coordinator. Knowledge and Skills: *Maintains the professional knowledge base needed to facilitate preparation of lab materials for contemporary nursing practice. Effectiveness in University Services: *Contributes to the SUNY Morrisville academic community through participation in division and campus committees and activities. *Participates in nursing events and activities including Orientation Boot Camp, recruitment events and accepted student days. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Associates degree Preferred Qualifications Healthcare experience strongly desired Strong computer skills adapting to technological changes RN degree preferred Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=195491": {
      "title": "Instructional Support Technician - School of Nursing",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Instructional Support Technician - School of Nursing SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Instructional Support Technician - School of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Instructional Support Technician - School of Nursing Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Dec 9, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 195491 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Instructional Support Technician- School of Nursing Budget Title : Instructional Support Technician Unit: UUP-8 Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL-3; $48,000 - 55,000 Duration: College Year (10 Month Schedule) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a Instructional Support Technician to assist our School of Nursing Faculty, Staff, and Students. The successful candidate for this position will have passion for supporting our next generation of nursing professionals, and the skills to help enhance learning experiences.  This person will work to ensure our nursing program meets our campus philosophy and mission, current nursing health care trends, and community and societal needs to prepare graduates for practice in complex, dynamic, multicultural health care environments Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Nursing Laboratory Support & Maintenance *Standardizes and prepares nursing lab supplies and materials (e.g. IV fluids, dressings, simulated medications) in accordance with program requirements. *Performs routine maintenance of nursing lab equipment including manikins, vital sign monitoring devices (such as blood pressure cuffs), and other equipment. *Sets up and breaks down lab stations for nursing lab teaching and practice sessions and prepares and resets equipment and environments for clinical simulations. *Assists Laboratory Coordinator with inventory of nursing lab supplies, consumables, and equipment; restocks labs prior to each semester. *Collaborate with the Campus Nursing Laboratory Coordinator in planning and scheduling to effectively utilize laboratory resources. *Collect and maintains statistics related to laboratory usage and communicates to the Campus Laboratory Coordinator. Knowledge and Skills *Maintains the professional knowledge base needed to facilitate preparation of lab materials for contemporary nursing practice Effectiveness in University Services *Contributes to the SUNY Morrisville academic community through participation in division and campus committees and activities. *Participates in nursing events and activities including Orientation Boot Camp, recruitment events and accepted student days. Continuing Growth: Engages in self-reflection and continues learning to improve lab practices that facilitate student learning. Additional Responsibilities for RN, BSN at IST level: * Under the direction of faculty assists students with nursing skills practice, instructs students in the skills laboratory setting, and assists with clinical simulations *Assist students with utilizing online learning resources. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications *RN degree *Bachelor's Degree *strong computer skills adapting to technological changes Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
