    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203357": {
      "title": "Plant Utilities Engineer I (NY HELPS) (Applicant Pool)",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Plant Utilities Engineer I (NY HELPS) (Applicant Pool) SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Plant Utilities Engineer I (NY HELPS) (Applicant Pool) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Plant Utilities Engineer I (NY HELPS) (Applicant Pool) Category: Civil Service and Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Aug 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203357 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Plant Utilities Engineer I Budget Title : Plant Utilities Engineer I Unit: CSEA-OSU; view our state benefits summary here ! Professional Rank and Salary Range: SG-14; $56,506 Duration: Calendar Year (12-month schedule) Shift: TBD, dependent on need. Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a Plant Utilities Engineer I. On an assigned shift, Plant Utilities Engineer I reports to a higher level Plant Utilities Engineer or other trades supervisor, and is responsible for the operation, repair, and maintenance of a variety of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and mechanical equipment inside and outside of a physical plant; may supervise lower-level staff including Plant Utilities Assistants, Facility Operations Assistants, and contractors; may assume responsibility for physical plant operations on off hours; and may supervise other trades positions and contractors on a project or emergency basis. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Operates, maintains, and repairs steam and hot water boilers, water supply and return systems, electronic and pneumatic combustion and heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) control systems, forced or induced draft fan systems, chiller systems, and other refrigeration equipment. Operates computers which control boiler operations, auxiliary equipment, and HVAC systems. Conducts boiler, HVAC, and water systems testing, analyzes results, and adds chemicals to maintain proper system functions. Balances air distribution systems, and maintains proper air temperature, humidity, freshness, and flow quality. Cleans, inspects, and maintains boilers, by performing chemical cleaning of equipment, repairing brickwork, replacing tubes, and maintaining boiler combustion and emissions. Performs chiller maintenance such as the cleaning of condenser tubes and evaporators, and the maintenance and repair of pumps, air compressors, steam systems, cooling towers, motors, and variable frequency drives. Performs maintenance and repair on various water and sewage pumping, filtration, and treatment equipment. Cleans, maintains, and repairs HVAC systems and equipment, calibrates controls, performs air testing and chemical treatment, and replaces air filters. Responds to mechanical, electrical, or plumbing calls; troubleshoots and coordinate necessary repairs. Maintains computerized energy management systems; troubleshoots problems; and identifies and replaces faulty equipment and devices. Identifies, recommends, and develops energy conservation projects and initiatives. May handle various types of hazardous materials; and respond to incidents having potential environmental impact and/or safety concerns, such as chemical spills, oil spills and blowouts; implements evacuation plans in emergency situations. May maintain right-to-know libraries, respond to inquiries, assess problems, and provide advice regarding incidents. May operate high or low voltage electrical distribution systems, steam, diesel and gas turbine generators, transformers and switch gears, load centers, motor control centers, panel boards, emergency power and lighting distribution systems, motor generator sets, and uninterrupted power supply systems. May supervise subordinate staff, including Plant Utilities Assistants, Facility Operations Assistants, contractors, and other trades staff. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications This title is part of the New York Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide Program (NY HELPS). For the duration of the NY HELPS Program, this title maybe filled via a non-competitive appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the minimum qualifications of the title for which they apply. At a future date (within one year of permanent appointment), it is expected employees hired under NY HELPS will have their non-competitive employment status converted to competitive status, without having to compete in an examination. Employees will then be afforded with all of the same rights and privileges of competitive class employees of New York State. While serving permanently in a NY HELPS title, employees may take part in any promotion examination for which they are qualified. NON-COMPETITIVE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (NY HELPS): Either 1. Graduate of heating, HVAC, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration apprenticeship program from the U.S. Air Force; Or 2. Must have been an enlisted machinery technician (MK) with the U.S. Coast Guard OR possession of a certificate as a Marine Engineer issued by the U.S. Coast Guard; Or 3. Must have been an enlisted power generation equipment repairer with the U.S. Army; Or 4. Must have been an enlisted gas turbine systems technician, submarine nuclear propulsion plant operator reactor control, utilities man, machinist mate, or engineman with the U.S. Navy; Or 5. Must have a Merchant Mariner's Document (MMD) and have been a qualified member of the engine department (QMED) as an oiler, fireman/water tender, refrigerating engineer or engineman with the U.S. Merchant Marine; Or 6. Completion of a New York State Department of Labor registered apprenticeship program for stationary engineers, plant maintenance (plumber/steamfitter), HVAC Mechanic or plant maintenance (refrigeration/AC) (See Note #1); Or 7. Possession of a High-Pressure Boiler Operating Engineer License or Stationary Engineer License; Or 8. A bachelor's degree in Facilities Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Marine Engineering; Or 9. Four years of full-time hands on experience in the maintenance and operation of commercial, industrial, institutional facility, computer applications of digital energy platforms and building analytics and/or performing diagnosis, repair of HVAC systems or boilers or auxiliary equipment; Or 10. Four years of full-time hands on experience in a residential setting performing diagnosis, operation, maintenance repair of HVAC systems or boilers or auxiliary equipment; Or 11. An associate's degree in HVAC AND two years of qualifying experience as described in EITHER qualification #9 or #10 above; Or 12. Completion of an HVAC certificate or diploma from a BOCES program (900 hours) OR completion of an approved certificate in HVAC, electrical, refrigeration, boiler operations and maintenance, or plumbing from an accredited technical school or technology college (See Note #2) AND two years of qualifying experience as described in EITHER qualification #9 or #10 above. Note #1 Information regarding qualifying New York State Department of Labor recognized apprenticeship programs can be found here: https://labor.ny.gov/apprenticeship/appindex.shtm [(External Link)] . Note # 2 Certification programs must be accredited by the Accrediting Commission of Career Schools and Colleges (ACCSC) or recognized by the New York State Education Department Bureau of Proprietary School Supervision (BPSS). Information on ACCSC accredited programs can be found here: http://www.accsc.org/ [(External Link)] . Information on BPSS recognized proprietary schools can be found here: http://www.acces.nysed.gov/bpss/welcome-career-training-proprietary-schools [(External Link)] . COMPETITIVE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (NON-NY HELPS): Candidates must have a reachable score on the Plant Utilities Engineer 1 Exam List OR Be a current NYS employee in a title eligible to transfer to Plant Utilities Engineer 1 OR Be a former NYS employee eligible for reinstatement to the title of Plant Utilities Engineer 1 *May be filled from a mandatory reemployment list if one is in effect at the time of appointment. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community, especially members of historically under-represented groups. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation.  If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application by as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Application materials are required to be submitted on-line at http://www.morrisville.edu/careers Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203349": {
      "title": "Facility Operations Assistant 1 (Applicant Pool)",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Facility Operations Assistant 1 (Applicant Pool) SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Facility Operations Assistant 1 (Applicant Pool) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Facility Operations Assistant 1 (Applicant Pool) Category: Civil Service and Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Aug 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203349 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Facility Operations Assistant 1 Budget Title: Facility Operations Assistant 1 Unit: CSEA-OSU Professional Rank and Salary Range: SG-6; $36,232 Duration: Calendar Year (12-month schedule) Schedule: TBD dependent on campus need; expectation is rotating 2nd and 3rd shifts. Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a Facility Operations Assistant 1 to serve as a flexible member of the Facilities Management team. The incumbent will perform a combination of custodial, receiving and material-handling, grounds maintenance, moving, event-support, delivery, and general facilities duties based on departmental and campus needs. This position is intended to provide support across multiple Facilities operations rather than remain permanently assigned to one functional area. Assignments may change daily, seasonally, or for longer periods depending on workload, staffing, weather conditions, campus events, and operational priorities. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Performs custodial duties in academic, administrative, residential, athletic, and other campus facilities, including vacuuming, sweeping, mopping, stripping and waxing floors; cleaning and disinfecting restrooms and fixtures; emptying trash and recycling; dusting; and cleaning windows, walls, furniture, and equipment. Assembles cleaning carts, prepares and uses cleaning solutions in accordance with manufacturer instructions, and monitors custodial supplies and equipment. Receives, unloads, inspects, sorts, records, stores, and distributes packages, equipment, supplies, furniture, and other materials delivered to the College. Loads and unloads trucks and delivery vehicles by physically handling materials or using pallet jacks, hand trucks, forklifts, and other material-handling equipment. Tracks and documents the receipt, storage, movement, and delivery of packages and materials and obtains signatures or other proof of delivery when required. Organizes and maintains receiving, warehouse, storage, surplus, and staging areas. Assists truck drivers and motor vehicle operators with pickups and deliveries and may operate campus vehicles to deliver mail, packages, equipment, supplies, furniture, and other materials. Performs general grounds maintenance, including mowing, trimming, raking, leaf and debris removal, brush clearing, planting, mulching, soil preparation, road and sidewalk maintenance, and general landscape cleanup. Removes snow and ice from sidewalks, building entrances, roadways, loading areas, parking lots, and other campus surfaces and applies salt, sand, or other approved deicing materials. Operates self-propelled and motorized equipment, including lawn mowers, snowblowers, utility vehicles, small trucks, tractors, forklifts, electric pallet jacks, and light construction or grounds equipment, when properly trained and authorized. Moves and arranges furniture, office equipment, records, supplies, partitions, and other materials for office relocations, residence hall operations, meetings, conferences, special events, and campus activities. Sets up and removes tables, chairs, podiums, staging, barriers, signs, and related equipment for campus events and activities. Assists higher-level maintenance, grounds, custodial, receiving, and trades staff with routine unskilled and semiskilled work, including transporting materials, preparing work areas, erecting ladders, cleaning gutters and drains, removing construction debris, preparing surfaces for painting, digging, loading and unloading materials, and cleaning work areas following completion of work. Performs routine building-support tasks, such as changing lamps, unclogging toilets and sinks, reporting damaged equipment or unsafe conditions, and assisting with minor repairs under appropriate supervision. Inspects assigned areas and reports building deficiencies, safety hazards, vandalism, damaged property, equipment malfunctions, and other conditions requiring attention. Assists with surplus-property activities, including moving, staging, organizing, inventorying, loading, and disposing of furniture and equipment in accordance with College procedures. May perform basic office-related duties associated with assigned work, including entering or recording deliveries, filing, photocopying, maintaining inventories, preparing simple reports, and documenting labor, materials, equipment use, and completed work. Provides courteous assistance and information to students, employees, visitors, vendors, and delivery personnel. May lead or provide direction to student employees, temporary staff, volunteers, or other assigned workers by explaining tasks, distributing supplies and equipment, and demonstrating proper work methods. May be temporarily assigned to any Facilities Management work group when operationally necessary, provided the assigned duties are consistent with the Facility Operations Assistant 1 title. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Labor Class: There are no education or experience qualifications for this class. Applicants must: Be physically able to perform the duties of the position, including repeated bending, reaching, lifting, carrying, pushing, pulling, standing, walking, climbing, and working indoors and outdoors under varying environmental and weather conditions. Be able to understand and carry out written and oral instructions. Possess and maintain a valid New York State driver's license appropriate for the vehicles operated. Be able and willing to perform custodial, receiving, grounds, moving, delivery, event-support, and general facilities assignments based on campus operational needs. Be able to lift and move heavy supplies, packages, furniture, equipment, and materials independently or with appropriate assistance and material-handling equipment. Be able to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Be available to work alternate shifts, weekends, holidays, overtime, and emergency call-ins when required. Obtain and maintain required campus authorizations or certifications for equipment operation, including forklifts, pallet jacks, utility vehicles, or other assigned equipment. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203342": {
      "title": "Trades Specialist Plumber & Steamfitter (SG-12)",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Trades Specialist Plumber & Steamfitter (SG-12) SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Trades Specialist Plumber & Steamfitter (SG-12) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Trades Specialist Plumber & Steamfitter (SG-12) Category: Civil Service and Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Aug 4, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203342 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Trades Specialist Plumber & Steamfitter Budget Title : Trades Specialist Plumber & Steamfitter Unit: CSEA-OSU Professional Rank and Salary Range: SG-12; $50,425 Duration: Calendar Year (12-month schedule) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a skilled Plumber & Steamfitter to join the Facilities Management Department. Under the general supervision of the Maintenance Supervisor, the successful candidate will perform journey-level plumbing and steamfitting work involving the installation, maintenance, troubleshooting, repair, replacement, testing, and modification of plumbing, heating, steam, condensate, compressed air, domestic water, sanitary, storm, natural gas, and other piping systems throughout the College. The successful candidate will support a diverse campus consisting of academic buildings, residence halls, athletic facilities, agricultural facilities, and central utility infrastructure while ensuring systems operate safely, reliably, and efficiently. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Install, maintain, troubleshoot, repair, and replace domestic water, sanitary sewer, storm drainage, natural gas, compressed air, steam, condensate, hot water, and related piping systems. Install, repair, replace, and maintain plumbing fixtures, faucets, valves, flush valves, water heaters, mixing valves, backflow prevention devices, pumps, drains, floor drains, cleanouts, and associated equipment. Perform steamfitting work involving steam and condensate piping, pressure reducing stations, steam traps, expansion joints, strainers, heat exchangers, valves, pumps, and related campus utility equipment. Install, modify, and repair copper, cast iron, PVC, CPVC, stainless steel, black iron, galvanized steel, PEX, and threaded, welded, soldered, brazed, grooved, or mechanical piping systems. Diagnose and repair leaks, blockages, piping failures, equipment malfunctions, and other plumbing and steam distribution problems. Perform preventive maintenance and inspections of plumbing and steam systems to maximize reliability and extend equipment life. Assist with the installation, replacement, and maintenance of mechanical equipment associated with plumbing and steam systems, including pumps, heat exchangers, domestic hot water systems, and related equipment. Read and interpret blueprints, piping schematics, specifications, equipment manuals, and shop drawings. Coordinate utility shutdowns and system isolations to minimize disruption to campus operations. Operate threading machines, pipe cutters, welding and brazing equipment, drain cleaning equipment, pipe fusion equipment, power tools, lifts, excavation equipment, and other specialized tools associated with the trade. Perform excavation, demolition, concrete removal and replacement, and restoration work associated with underground utility repairs. Assist contractors and other Facilities trades on renovation, rehabilitation, and capital improvement projects. Maintain accurate maintenance records and document work performed using the College's computerized maintenance management system (CMMS). Respond to plumbing, steam, and utility emergencies during normal working hours and after-hours as required. Maintain a safe work environment and comply with applicable OSHA regulations, New York State Uniform Code, applicable plumbing codes, campus safety procedures, and environmental requirements. Perform other duties consistent with the Plumber & Steamfitter title as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Non-competitive: Four years of full-time experience in plumbing under a skilled tradesperson; which would provide training equivalent to that given in a training, apprenticeship, or equivalent program, OR an equivalent combination of experience and training gained by completion of technical courses in plumbing at a school, institute, or branch of the Armed Services; OR successful completion of the two-year Trades Specialist (Plumber & Steamfitter) traineeship or a two-year plumbing training, apprenticeship, or equivalent program* such as the New York State Civil Service Employees Association-Partnership Applied Skilled Trades Traineeship and Certificate Program * Successful completion of the traineeship and the training program includes a total of 288 hours of trade-specific classroom instruction, 45 hours of technical math course work, 45 hours of technical communications course work, and 15 hours of blueprint/schematic reading course work. Course work must be completed with an average of \"C\" or better. Additionally, successful completion of the traineeship also includes 4,000 hours of on-the-job training. Operational needs: Possess and maintain a valid New York State driver's license. Be physically able to perform journey-level plumbing and steamfitting work, including lifting heavy materials, climbing ladders, working at heights, working underground, working in confined spaces, and working indoors and outdoors under varying weather conditions. Be able to read and interpret blueprints, piping diagrams, technical manuals, and written instructions. Demonstrate the ability to safely operate tools, equipment, and machinery commonly used in the plumbing and steamfitting trades. Be available to work overtime, alternate shifts, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-ins as required to support campus operations. Be able to work independently and collaboratively in a customer-service-oriented environment. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202444": {
      "title": "Service & Repair Mechanic (Electronics) - SG-12 (NY HELPS)",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Service & Repair Mechanic (Electronics) - SG-12 (NY HELPS) SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Service & Repair Mechanic (Electronics) - SG-12 (NY HELPS) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Service & Repair Mechanic (Electronics) - SG-12 (NY HELPS) Category: Civil Service and Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Jul 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 202444 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Service & Repair Mechanic (Electronics) Budget Title : Service & Repair Mechanic (Electronics) Unit: CSEA-OSU Professional Rank and Salary Range: SG-12,  $50,425 Duration: Calendar Year (this position works year-round) Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a Service and Repair Mechanic (Electronics) for the installation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of campus electronic and low voltage systems. These systems include fire alarm systems, electronic access control systems, video surveillance systems, emergency communication systems, building automation systems, and related communication infrastructure. The position supports reliable operation of critical campus infrastructure and assists in maintaining compliance with applicable codes and safety standards. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Install, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair electronic systems including fire alarm systems, electronic access control systems, video surveillance systems, emergency communication devices, and building automation systems. Perform routine inspections, testing, and preventive maintenance of electronic equipment to ensure reliable operation and compliance with applicable codes and standards. Diagnose equipment failures using appropriate testing instruments, wiring diagrams, and technical documentation. Repair or replace defective components, wiring, and system devices. Assist with installation and commissioning of new electronic and low voltage systems. Maintain records of inspections, repairs, and testing activities. Install and maintain low voltage wiring associated with building systems including controls, generators, and communication equipment. Coordinate with contractors and vendors during system installation and repair activities. Operate campus vehicles and transport tools and equipment to job locations. Follow applicable safety procedures and electrical safety standards. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Four years of full-time experience in the installation, maintenance, and repair of electronic equipment. Substitution: An associate's degree in electronic technology, or successful completion of a two-year technical professional certification program in the electronics field may be substituted for two years of the required experience; -OR- Graduation from a high school technical electronics education program recognized by the New York State Education Department as meeting the standards for technical education may be substituted for one year of the required experience. Examples of qualifying experience include work involving: Fire alarm systems Security or access control systems Video surveillance systems Communication systems Building automation or control systems Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with fire alarm systems Experience working with electronic access control systems Experience working with video surveillance systems Experience working with building automation systems Experience installing and troubleshooting low voltage wiring Ability to read and interpret electrical schematics and technical manuals Experience working in institutional or campus environments Familiarity with National Electrical Code and National Fire Protection Association Codes and Standards Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=196632": {
      "title": "University Police Officer I",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: University Police Officer I SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: University Police Officer I Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details University Police Officer I Category: Civil Service and Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: University Police Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Jan 21, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 196632 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: University Police Officer 1 State Title: University Police Officer 1 Department: University Police Bargaining Unit: PBANYS; view our state benefits summary here ! Professional Rank and Salary Range: SG-14; $64,796 Duration: Calendar Year (this position follows a 12-month schedule) Shift : Rotating Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a University Police Officer I to support our University Police department. University Police Officers enforce all New York State and local laws and the Student Code of Conduct on the grounds of the State University of New York. University Police Officers are charged with full police officer powers under Criminal Procedure Law, Section 1.20(34)(s) and are responsible for the performance of the full range of professional police duties. University Police Officers assist other Local, State and Federal police officers with investigations and may collect evidence, question witnesses or testify in court in connection with alleged criminal actions. University Police Officers are actively involved in campus communities and activities including educating community members on such topics as personal safety, risk awareness, crime prevention, alcohol awareness, sexual assault prevention and other community safety issues. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Patrols an assigned area on foot, on a bicycle or motor scooter, in a car or by other means to deter criminal activity by means of presence and witness and to detect fires and other dangerous situations. Responds to calls for assistance from fellow officers or from any member of the campus community to insure that persons and property are adequately protected; and may respond to situations involving but not restricted to burglaries, robberies, thefts, criminal trespass, assaults, criminal mischief, medical emergencies, accidents, vehicle and traffic violations, fires and unusual situations. Reports to the scene of the crime, accident or other disturbance in order to halt crimes in progress, arrest violators, maintain order and arrange for the appropriate care of injured persons. May apply resuscitators, administer first aid and summon ambulances. Conducts initial investigations of incidents in order to preserve and gather evidence; interviews witnesses, complainants and suspects and confers with fellow officers to ascertain nature and severity of situation; reports results of investigations to supervisor as directed and may testify in court. Regulates pedestrian and vehicular traffic. May enforce vehicle and traffic laws in order to prevent dangerous situations from arising. Directs traffic at intersections, crosswalks and other critical points during peak traffic periods; stops persons violating the vehicle and traffic law; issues warnings, tickets and summonses; patrols parking lots and campus roadways; tickets cars parked in violation of campus rules. Controls the movement and activity of crowds at concerts, sports events and other gatherings; staffs entrance ways to prevent gate crashing and over-crowding of facilities; breaks up fights and other altercations, operates screening devices such as a magnetometer or x-ray machine to inspect individuals and carry in items for prohibited items. On assignment as Desk Officer. Receives and interprets incoming communications, including, but not limited to radio and telephone calls, and e-mail messages from officers and other members of the campus community. Dispatches officers to the scenes of incidents and irregularities. Issues parking permits and collects fees and fines. Utilizes electronic devices such as a personal computer, video recorder or camera to record and view information. On assignment to K-9 Corps. May patrol high crime rate areas and shifts with a trained police dog. Gives commands to dog to halt fleeing criminals, disperse crowds and guard arrested persons. May give demonstrations to interested groups both on and off campus, of the uses, effectiveness and safety of police dogs as a law enforcement tool. Responsible for care, feeding and maintenance of a police dog. Prepares a variety of shift summary reports, logs and records covering activities of a criminal or unusual nature and other security related activities. May deliver a variety of in-service training and/or community educational programs. Obtains proper certification and maintain re-certification in a variety of training areas, such as defensive tactics, use of force and firearms instruction. Serves as a Field Training Officer or as an instructor at a Basic Police School, Police Academy or other location as directed. Provides training and education to University Police personnel, other law enforcement officers, government personnel and the public, and engages in crime prevention activities such as, but not limited to Crime Prevention Surveys or Operation ID. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Open Competitive: Must be reachable on current University Police Officer 1, SG-14 list or currently hold the title of University Police Officer 1, SG-14, or a title from which transfer is appropriate. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community, especially members of historically under-represented groups. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation.  If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application by as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Application materials are required to be submitted on-line at http://www.morrisville.edu/careers Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=195331": {
      "title": "Cleaner (Applicant Pool)",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Cleaner (Applicant Pool) SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Cleaner (Applicant Pool) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Cleaner (Applicant Pool) Category: Civil Service and Support Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Dec 4, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 195331 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Cleaner Budget Title :                      Cleaner Unit: CSEA-OSU-03; view our generous state benefits summary here ! Professional Rank and Salary Range: SG-5; $34,312 (annual salary) Duration: Calendar Year Schedule (this position works year-round) Application Pool: This position accepts applications on an ongoing basis due to continuous hiring needs. If you are interested, please apply and kindly note that we review applications as needed within the team! Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a cleaner. This is a launch pad into a career with SUNY Morrisville! Cleaners perform a wide range of cleaning tasks to maintain assigned areas in State buildings, and surrounding grounds and walkways. Incumbents work independently or as part of a cleaning team in a variety of settings, such as administrative office, classroom, laboratory, living, treatment, and other work areas. Primary Responsibilities : Performs a variety of cleaning tasks in assigned areas. Collects and empties trash and recycling in accordance with cleaning schedules; cleans and/or removes hazardous or misplaced items, waste, and spills; and disposes, transports, or places such in appropriate receptacles and locations, following proper cleaning procedures. Assembles cleaning carts according to assigned tasks; and prepares, mixes, and dilutes cleaning solutions following manufacturer directions. Washes floors, corridors, stairwells, walls, partitions, and windows using mops, detergents, brushes, and other cleaning devices. Vacuums, strips and waxes floors, and shampoos carpets, using manual or mechanical equipment. Scrubs and cleans showers and restrooms, including toilets, sinks, and drains, using hand-operated equipment and cleaning agents. Replaces light bulbs, and dusts or washes light fixtures and high places, such as ceilings, using ladders, other appropriate equipment, and tools. Polishes wood and metal surfaces, fixtures, furniture, and equipment. Monitors cleaning supplies and equipment; and notifies supervisor of supply levels, equipment malfunction, and/or maintenance issues observed during cleaning. Replaces, cleans, and/or hangs building fixtures and decorative items, such as curtains, blinds, and pictures. Moves, and arranges furniture and equipment in connection with cleaning tasks or in preparation for meetings, events, and other activities. May be required to follow specialized disinfectant, waste disposal, and cleanliness standards in performing cleaning tasks; remove snow and salt walkways; clean sidewalks, drives, and grounds; mow lawns, using mechanical and manual equipment; perform routine laundry tasks; and change bed linens. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Must possess a valid NYS drivers license Cleaners must be physically able to perform the tasks of the position and understand and carry out written and oral instructions Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit the required materials directly through the online job application posting. Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204803": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor in Equine Reproduction- Tenure Track",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Instructor or Assistant Professor in Equine Reproduction- Tenure Track SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Instructor or Assistant Professor in Equine Reproduction- Tenure Track Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Instructor or Assistant Professor in Equine Reproduction- Tenure Track Category: Full-time Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Agriculture, Business & Technology Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Sep 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 204803 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Instructor or Assistant Professor in Equine Reproduction- Tenure Track Faculty Budget Title : Instructor or Assistant Professor - Tenure Track Faculty Unit: 08-UUP; view our generous state benefits package here! https://www.suny.edu/benefits/benefit-summaries/benefits-at-a-glance---uup-full-time/ Professional Rank and Salary Range: $55,000 - 65,000, DOE Duration: 10-month Academic Year Faculty Position Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville seeks applicants for a 10-month tenure track Equine Reproduction faculty position with responsibilities of teaching courses in the Equine Science Program offered in the Equine Science and Management Associate of Applied Science Degree and Equine Science Bachelor of Technology Degree. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : 1. Curriculum & Classroom Instruction - Faculty's primary responsibilities are to the department's teaching mission by teaching a range of Equine Reproduction courses in the equine science curriculum. Courses taught could be: Equine Reproduction and Breeding Management (Introductory and Advanced), Artificial Insemination and Animal Genetics. Instructional areas may include introductory courses like: Stable Management, Fitting and Marketing, Equine Judging, Young horse handling, to more advanced courses such as Equine Business Management, Internship orientation. Experiential Learning: Heavy emphasis on \"hands-on\" labs, working closely with Instructional Support Assistants (ISAs) to ensure students aren't just reading about horses, but actually handling and working with them. Address emerging and traditional topics in equine reproduction, breeding farm management (stallion, mare and young stock) and demonstrate proper handling and care related those topics to students and stakeholders. Program Development: Team-based collaboration with Equine Science department faculty/staff to support the course development and program evaluation for industry relevance, entrepreneurial mindset to keep the curriculum \"industry-ready.\" 2. Student Mentorship & Service - Student Support: Academic advising, career counseling, recruitment, and potential supervision of student clubs. Internship Coordination: Bridge between classroom and industry with internship program. Outreach opportunities may include the dedicated efforts of supporting equine program stakeholders. University Service: Collegial contributions to academic community though service at departmental, college, and/or university levels will be expected. 3. Herd & Operations Management - Animal Oversight: Assist with management of health and daily care of both college-owned and client-owned horses. Administrative Responsibilities: Budgeting, recordkeeping, and managing sales/procurement. Industry Liaison: Building relationships with regional equine professionals to bring in new program clients, animals and secure internships. Salary supplementation: Extra service or additional funded opportunities through SUNY Morrisville: Candidate can seek grant-funded research opportunities, coaching of Western IHSA Equestrian Team and campus teaching extra service. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Instructor rank - Bachelor's degree in equine or closely related fields is required; with minimum 5 years of industry working experience or currently in pursuit of Master's degree. Assistant Professor rank - a Master's degree in equine or closely related fields is required and a higher degree (PhD or DVM) is preferred. Prefer experience teaching or working as an instructor, strong interpersonal and communication (both written and oral) skills and an understanding of current equine industry practices. Equine Experience: Successful applicant should have experience in some of the following areas - Young horse handling and training, Breeding management (Stallion and/or Broodmare mgmt.), and/or and willingness to expand the knowledge of students in an all-around equine management, reproduction, training and rehabilitation program. Applicant should demonstrate the potential for 1) excellent teaching, 2) academic and career advisement of our undergraduate students, 3) contribution to department's continuing and developing instructional, entrepreneurial and recruitment activities, and 4) effective teamwork within a diverse array of students, colleagues, and equine professionals. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=201562": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Renewable Energy - Tenure Track",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Renewable Energy - Tenure Track SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Renewable Energy - Tenure Track Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Renewable Energy - Tenure Track Category: Full-time Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Agriculture, Business & Technology Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Jun 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 201562 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Assistant Professor of Renewable Energy - Tenure Track Budget Title :  Assistant Professor Unit: UUP-08; view our units state benefits summary here! Professional Rank and Salary Range: $60,000 - $70,000 Duration: 10-month Academic Year Faculty Position About our program: This position supports an established renewable energy program with strong emphasis on technical, workforce-oriented education.  Courses are structured to combine theory with hands-on application, preparing students for careers in solar, wind, electrical systems, thermal systems, and energy infrastructure. Read more about our program by visiting our website, linked here: https://www.morrisville.edu/areas-of-study/renewable-energy Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Renewable Energy to support a growing, hands-on technical program.  This position focuses on undergraduate teaching in applied renewable energy systems, with an emphasis on solar photovoltaic systems, wind energy, electrical systems, and grid-integrated technologies. The successful candidate will deliver lectures and laboratory instruction, contribute to curriculum development, and support workforce training initiatives aligned with industry needs. This is a teaching-focused position, which typically includes 14-17 instruction contact hours per week (lectures and labs).  Most classes are structured with 2 lecture hours and 2-3 lab hours weekly. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Teach undergraduate courses in renewable energy systems through applied, lab-based instruction. Deliver instruction in areas such as: - Wind energy systems: resource assessment, system installation, maintenance, and troubleshooting - Solar photovoltaic systems: site assessment, installation, system design (residential to utility scale), and code compliance - Electrical systems and controls: power electronics, monitoring systems (e.g., SCADA), system protection, and structured troubleshooting methods - Renewable energy system design and development: including system sizing, load analysis, permitting considerations, and performance optimization - Advanced energy systems and grid technologies: smart grids, energy storage, microgrids, and grid integration of renewable systems Develop and revise curriculum to reflect current industry standards, codes, and emerging technologies. Support workforce development and technical training programs. Engage with industry partners to maintain program relevance and expand opportunities for students. Participate in student advising, program assessment, and campus service. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications - Master's degree (or higher) in renewable energy, engineering, engineering technology, or a closely related field - Demonstrated ability to teach applied technical content at the college or workforce training level, including laboratory environments - Hands-on industry experience in one or more of the following areas: - Solar photovoltaic systems (installation, design, or commissioning) - Wind energy systems (installation, operation, or maintenance) - Energy storage systems (installation, design, or commissioning) - Electrical systems, controls, or power systems relevant to energy applications Preferred Qualifications: - Industry certifications (e.g., NABCEP, OSHA, or similar) - Experience with tools such as AutoCAD, energy modeling software, or monitoring/control platforms - Experience with National Electrical Code (NEC) - Prior experience with applied, project-based, or lab-intensive teaching - Engagement in workforce development, grant-funded initiatives, or industry partnerships - Proficiency in using learning management systems (e.g., Brightspace, Blackboard) Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
