    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=193685": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track) SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor, Nursing (Tenure Track) Category: Full-time Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Morrisville, NY Posted: Oct 8, 2025 Closes: Jul 6, 2040 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Position ID: 193685 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus/Budget Title: Assistant Professor Unit: 08-UUP, view our generous state benefits summary here ! Professional Rank and Salary Range: $62,000+ Duration: This position is full time, following a 10-month academic year. Enjoy summers off! Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking a dynamic and forward-thinking individual to join our campus as an Assistant Professor for our Nursing Department. As a member of our faculty, you will play a crucial role in shaping the next generation of nursing professionals by integrating modern technology and innovative teaching methods into the nursing curriculum. This position offers an exciting opportunity to combine your passion for nursing education with your expertise in leveraging technology to enhance the learning experience. This program is an ACEN Accredited Associate Degree Nursing program enrolling approximately 150 students, 50 of which are at the Norwich Campus. Primary Responsibilities Include, But Are Not Limited to: Curriculum Development: Collaborate with the nursing department to develop and update curriculum that reflects the latest advancements in healthcare technology and aligns with industry standards. Integrate technology-driven teaching strategies and active learning methods to engage students and promote critical thinking. Classroom Instruction: Deliver high-quality instruction to nursing students utilizing a variety of teaching methods, including lectures, virtual simulations, online modules, and interactive multimedia resources. Foster an inclusive and collaborative learning environment that encourages student engagement and participation. Coursework includes teaching theory and clinical in areas that include medical-surgical, psychiatric, pediatric, and obstetrical nursing. Student Mentorship: Provide guidance and support to students throughout their educational journey, including recruiting students to join our program, academic advising, career counseling, and promoting professional development. Foster a student-centered approach that emphasizes individual growth and prepares students for the challenges of modern healthcare settings. The successful candidate for this position will be a team player and open to continuous improvement! We are willing to provide training and mentorship to motivated candidates! Travel to off-campus sites is required. Future teaching assignments could potentially include distance learning, evenings, weekends, and offsite locations. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: A Master's Degree (or higher) in Nursing Current license as a registered nurse (RN) Recent nursing experience Strong computer skills and ability to adapt to technology changes. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage and motivate students from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in teaching, curriculum development, and program evaluation. Membership in professional organizations Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community, especially members of historically under-represented groups. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application by as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Application materials are required to be submitted on-line at http://www.morrisville.edu/careers Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission) Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206246": {
      "title": "Senior Counselor",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Senior Counselor SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Senior Counselor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Counselor Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: SUNY EOC Locations: Syracuse, NY Posted: Oct 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 206246 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Senior Counselor Budget Title : Senior Counselor Unit: UUP Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL-4 $67,375 Duration: 12 Month Calendar Year Brief Description of Duties: The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (SEOC) is looking for a full-time Senior Counselor to provide counseling, case management, crisis support and referral services to our adult learners. Many of our students are dealing with issues such as housing, food, childcare, transportation or mental health that make it harder to stay in school. The Senior Counselor helps students work through these barriers so they can complete their programs and move on to college or employment. SEOC is part of the State University of New York (SUNY) and serves adults and out-of-school youth age 16 and older. We offer high school equivalency (HSE) preparation, college preparation, workforce training and career services. * This Position is located in Syracuse NY Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Counseling and Case Management Provide case management, short-term individual and group counseling, and advisement to students facing economic, housing, childcare, mental health or other barriers. Handle the Center's more complex and difficult cases. Complete intake and needs assessments and develop individual service, education and career plans with faculty and Student Services staff. Provide crisis intervention, risk assessment and mental health screening, and refer students to medical, mental health, community and social service providers as needed. Connect students with resources for food, housing, childcare, transportation and other needs. Monitor at-risk students and work with instructors on early intervention to improve retention and completion. Complete progress reports and keep accurate, confidential records in each student's file (Banner). Assist with student conduct matters according to the EOC Student Handbook. Provide follow-up support to former students as they move into college or employment. Workshops and Outreach Consult with faculty and staff about students of concern. Plan and lead workshops for students and staff on topics such as stress management, study skills and wellness. Take part in orientations, open houses, information sessions and other recruitment and retention activities. Intern Supervision Supervise graduate interns placed at SEOC, including Syracuse University School of Social Work interns, through weekly supervision, learning agreements and evaluations. Serve as Syracuse University field instructor if eligible, and act as backup contact for the Center's internship agreements. Assign and oversee intern caseloads. Disability Accommodations Serve as the Center's contact for student accommodation requests under the ADA and Section 504. Review documentation and coordinate academic and testing accommodations with instructors. Keep accommodation records confidential and separate from other student files. Other Help develop Student Services procedures and provide information for required reports. Serve on committees and attend trainings as appropriate. Perform other related duties as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in social work, mental health counseling, counseling, psychology or a closely related field from an accredited program. New York State license as an LMSW, LCSW, LMHC or Licensed Psychologist, or eligibility to obtain licensure within 6 months of hire. Two years of professional experience in counseling, case management, crisis intervention or related student support work. Strong record-keeping and organizational skills and the ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to work well with faculty, staff and community partners. Availability for occasional evening or weekend events. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with people from diverse backgrounds and underserved communities is strongly preferred. Master of Social Work (MSW) from a CSWE-accredited program with a current NYS LMSW or LCSW license. Eligibility to serve as a Syracuse University School of Social Work field instructor. Experience supervising interns or other staff. Experience in adult education, Educational Opportunity Programs, community colleges or workforce development. Experience with risk assessment and crisis intervention. Knowledge of ADA, Section 504 and Title IX. Experience leading workshops or group programs. Experience with electronic student records (Banner a plus). Bilingual or multilingual ability. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
    },
    "https://morrisville.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206254": {
      "title": "Director of Instructional Support",
      "description": "SUNY Morrisville\nJob Posting: Director of Instructional Support SUNY Morrisville \n\tJob Posting: Director of Instructional Support Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Instructional Support Category: Administrative and Professional Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: SUNY EOC Locations: Syracuse, NY Posted: Oct 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 206254 Share About SUNY Morrisville: About SUNY Morrisville: SUNY Morrisville , a college that leverages the expansive resources of the State University of New York, is a model of innovative applied education. Located in scenic Central New York, the college offers students hands-on, experiential learning in modern classrooms and specialized facilities, many of which are rare or one-of-a-kind in higher education. Morrisville's over 2,000 students - who come from diverse backgrounds across the state, nation, and world - choose from over 50 combined associate, bachelor's, and master's degree and certificate programs in a variety of disciplines, including agriculture, technology, business, social sciences, and the liberal arts. At Morrisville, motivated students work alongside talented faculty members - many with field experience - to imagine, build, and test practical, sustainable solutions to some of the fundamental questions confronting our global economy. As home of the Mustangs, SUNY Morrisville boasts 17 intercollegiate athletics programs which compete at the NCAA Division III level. The Morrisville campus is equidistant - roughly 30 miles - to the major cities of Syracuse and Utica; it is a half-hour drive from the New York State Thruway with easy access to Albany (two hours), Rochester (two hours), Buffalo (three hours) and New York City (four hours). The Norwich Campus of SUNY Morrisville, located 30 miles south of the Morrisville Campus, has been serving the Norwich community and the surrounding areas for more than 46 years, offering students a variety of degree options serving commuter students in career and technical fields. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center (EOC), administered by SUNY Morrisville, provides the community of Syracuse with innovative academic programs leading to higher education as well as vocational training programs leading to gainful employment and economic self-sufficiency. SUNY Morrisville has a highly diverse student population, which is one of the institution's great strengths. SUNY Morrisville is committed to equity and inclusion in all aspects of hiring and employment. The college recognizes the importance of maintaining and strengthening the diversity of student, faculty, and staff at the institution, which is essential to the success of students and graduates in an increasingly global environment. Job Description: Campus Title: Director of Instructional Support Budget Title: Director of Instructional Resources Unit: UUP-08 Professional Rank and Salary Range: SL-6 (Appendix A Title), $98,763 Duration: Calendar Year (this position works year-round); 8:30am-5pm *This position is located in Syracuse, NY (Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center) ABOUT THE SYRACUSE EOC The SEOC is part of a statewide network of ten Educational Opportunity Centers governed by the SUNY University Center for Academic and Workforce Development (UCAWD). We are committed to serving historically underrepresented communities and believe that education is one of the most powerful tools for long-term economic and social mobility. The Syracuse Educational Opportunity Center has been opening doors for adults in the Greater Syracuse area for decades. As a tuition-free program of the State University of New York, we serve people who are working toward their high school equivalency, preparing for college, learning English, or training for a new career. Brief Description of Duties: SUNY Morrisville is seeking an experienced adult education and workforce development leader who genuinely believes in the mission of adult education and understands the unique challenges our students face. The Director of Instructional Support and Workforce Development leads all instructional programming at SEOC. A central part of the role is instructional leadership: helping our instructors strengthen their teaching so that it meets the needs of adult learners who arrive with a wide range of academic levels, language backgrounds, work histories and life responsibilities. SEOC's workforce development programs have grown significantly: from 2024-25 to 2025-26, registrations rose from 380 to 493 and job placements rose from 14 to 91. The Director will guide the continued growth and improvement of these programs, maintain the quality and compliance of our High School Equivalency, College Preparation and ESOL programs, oversee the ATTAIN Lab and Tutoring Lab, and supervise instructional faculty and staff. The Director reports to the Associate Executive Director and serves on the senior leadership team. Primary Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Instructional Leadership and Faculty Development Observe classes regularly and give instructors practical, constructive feedback on their teaching, with a focus on what helps adult learners stay engaged, make progress and complete Lead ongoing professional development, not just compliance training, that builds instructors' skills in adult learning, including differentiated and contextualized instruction for learners at different academic and English language levels Recruit, hire, supervise and evaluate full-time instructors, adjunct workforce instructors, the Workforce Development Coordinator and instructional support staff, building a teaching staff that brings the right academic and industry credentials and reflects the communities we serve Create a culture where faculty and staff feel supported, heard and accountable; address performance issues directly and constructively; manage schedules and workloads Workforce Development Programs Lead the continuous improvement of SEOC's current workforce programs in construction, manufacturing, healthcare, security and office administration, and develop new programs as labor market demand warrants Prepare and maintain a current Instructional Program Plan (IPP), including labor market analysis, for every activated program, and obtain UCAWD pre-approval before implementing any new or substantially changed program (Policies #2025003 and 2024004-R3) Ensure workforce curricula build in industry-recognized certifications and, where possible, applied learning such as work experience, internships and pre-apprenticeship pathways Work with the Workforce Development Coordinator and employer partners to strengthen curriculum input, work-based learning and hiring of program completers Academic and Foundation Programs Maintain the quality and compliance of High School Equivalency Preparation, College Preparation, ESOL and foundation programs, including placement testing and educational gains measurement under UCAWD policy Build clear pathways from HSE, ESOL and foundation programs into workforce training and college Manage the academic calendar, scheduling and course assignments, and oversee the ATTAIN Lab and Tutoring Lab Student Success, Data and Compliance Work with Admissions, College and Career Services, Workforce Advisors and Student Success Coaches to improve attendance, retention and completion Monitor enrollment, completion, certification and job placement data monthly; ensure accurate, timely entry in Banner; and lead improvement plans when outcomes fall short Prepare the instructional components of the Operational Plan, program reviews and the Annual Operational Review Meeting (AORM) by UCAWD deadlines *As the Director grows into the role, responsibilities are expected to expand to include articulation agreements with SUNY and local colleges, the College Connections Initiative (CCI), grant and workforce funding proposals, and representing SEOC at statewide EOC and UCAWD convenings. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Adult Education, Workforce Development, Career and Technical Education, Education, Human Resource or Organizational Development, Public Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution At least three years of supervisory or administrative experience in workforce development, career and technical education, job training or adult education, with direct responsibility for program design, staff and outcomes Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities, regulatory timelines and a busy team Preferred Qualifications Experience observing, coaching or providing professional development to instructors, particularly in adult learning Experience working with adult learners or economically and educationally disadvantaged populations in a community-based, workforce or postsecondary setting Experience developing, revising or managing workforce training programs aligned to labor market data and industry-recognized credentials Experience building employer or industry partnerships that lead to student placement Experience with data systems and outcome tracking; familiarity with Banner Familiarity with SUNY EOC or UCAWD processes such as program approval, IPPs and the AORM Industry or training experience in a high-demand sector such as healthcare, skilled trades, manufacturing or security Bilingual or multilingual skills, especially in Spanish, Arabic, Somali or other languages spoken widely in the Syracuse community Familiarity with trauma-informed and strengths-based approaches in adult education *We encourage applicants who do not meet every preferred qualification to apply. SEOC provides onboarding in UCAWD policy, Banner and EOC reporting. Additional Information: SUNY Morrisville is committed to creating a vibrant community enriched by diverse perspectives, talents and experiences, and prohibits discrimination in employment based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, physical capability, age, creed, sexual identity, veteran status, and economic means.  We encourage applications from candidates who share this commitment and will contribute to the diversity of our college community. AA/EEO/ADA In accordance with the \"Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act\" institutions of higher education are required to prepare an annual report containing information on campus security policies and campus statistics. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by SUNY Morrisville; and on property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and other matters. You can obtain a printed copy of this report by contacting SUNY Morrisville University Police at (315) 684-6410, Office of Student Rights and Responsibilities at (315) 684-6070, Office of Human Resources at (315) 684-6038 and or by accessing the following web site: https://www.morrisville.edu/contact/offices/university-police/clery-act Application Instructions: Application Deadline: Although applications will be accepted until the position is filled, candidates should submit their application as soon as possible, to assure optimal consideration. Application Procedure: Applicants must submit all required materials directly through the online job application posting. Application Materials: Please provide Cover Letter, Resume, and at least three employment references (we will not contact references without prior permission). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Suny Morrisville 80 Eaton St, Morrisville, NY 13408"
